From 7636bb2fa95962647f5147338392b3163b75f37e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Matthias=20M=C3=BCnch?= <claude@djbase.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:52:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libcryptossh: entropy pool for randfill(), bebbosshkeygen
 fixes

randfill() mixed rand(), the DateStamp tick and the beam position - a few
dozen bits of entropy at best ("not cryptographically secure" said the
comment). It produces the ed25519 secret keys of bebbosshkeygen and the
ephemeral x25519 keys of every session, so both could be recovered with
moderate effort.

randpool.cpp: a SHA-512 pool fed with E-clock time stamps and beam
positions sampled across task switches, exec dispatch/idle counters,
free memory and a seed file ENVARC:.ssh/random_seed that is mixed in and
replaced on every first use. Output is SHA-512(pool | counter), the pool
is hashed forward after every call and gets a fresh time stamp on each.

bebbosshkeygen:
- the argument line is only flushed from a console; a redirected stdin
  is read unbuffered (it starts with the injected argument line, and
  flushing it seeks before the start of the file)
- write errors are detected, a truncated key file is deleted, exit 10
- the secret key material is cleared before exit, ge_new_keypair_ed25519
  clears the expanded secret on its stack
---
 Makefile               |   2 +-
 src/bebbosshkeygen.cpp |  98 +++++++++++++-----
 src/ed25519s.cpp       |   3 +
 src/rand.c             |  24 ++---
 src/randpool.cpp       | 222 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 309 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/randpool.cpp

